From ee00e9759dc4722e524aca0a0ed7903fe6c44826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:54:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/45] wifi: ath12k: bring peach up in mission mode

Cold-boot mode 7 and mission mode 0 both time out after the
firmware enters RDDM. The aux download is still rejected.

(Ported from the dodge v6.16 bring-up tree.)

Signed-off-by: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c | 9 ++-------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
index 1080f4864..653f07eb8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -4562,14 +4562,9 @@ static void ath12k_qmi_driver_event_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 			clear_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH,
 				  &ab->dev_flags);
-			/* Cold boot sends mode 7 before ini and cfg. With
-			 * skip_tme, take the normal path so those go out.
+			/* Cold boot mode 7 is where the aux MAC wakeup asserts.
+			 * Mission mode sends ini and cfg first.
 			 */
-			if (ab->id.device == 0x110e && ab->qmi.cal_done == 0 &&
-			    !ath12k_skip_tme) {
-				ath12k_qmi_process_coldboot_calibration(ab);
-				break;
-			}
 			ret = ath12k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(ab);
 			if (!ret)
 				set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FW_READY_COMPLETE,
-- 
